# Generated by governance model version 5. Only the generator changes this file.
"""Merge watch: records misses after merges as `miss` issues, and never blocks anything.

The workflow `.github/workflows/merge-watch.yml` runs this script from the default branch's
checkout. It is never a required check. It reads the event, then GitHub through `gh api`,
and opens one miss record per miss, in the format `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` gives
(Miss records), labelled `miss`.

On `push` to the default branch, a bounded event list is reconciled with the paginated
comparison of its before and after SHAs. An incomplete range is reported with its refs;
commits established by the event or recovered pages are still judged. Push runs post confirmed
misses as they go, honor GitHub's rate-limit delays and report where the audit stopped if its
time or retry budget runs out. For each pushed commit:

- the merged PR is the one whose squash commit it is. A commit that is only part of a merged
  PR's history is left to that PR's merge commit; a commit with no merged PR at all records a
  process miss, `push-without-pr`;
- a `Reverts:` line in the merged PR's body records an escape, `revert`, naming the reverted
  commit's PR;
- every review missing from the merged PR's head by its declared tier records one process
  miss, `missing-review`, listing each missing review by its Merge summary kind
  (`docs/agents/review.md`, Merge summary), then `merge-summary`. The tier requires
  `self-verification` and `merge-summary` at every tier, `bot-1` from medium,
  and `reviewer` at high:
  - **the Merge summary**: the historical agent account's newest comment titled
    `## Merge summary: <tier> at <sha>` for the declared tier and head. From v5, use all 40 hex
    digits. Known v1–v4 bases use the first seven, including a v4-to-v5 Upgrade.
    The second line lists the reviews. From v5, check each listed bot and Reviewer as well
    as the tier minimum. A missing required declaration is a `merge-summary` miss;
  - **a bot slot** is filled by a completed review on the head from a provider enabled in the
    record at the merge's base, the commit before the squash commit. A PR can't lower its own
    requirements by changing that list. When GitHub answers that the base holds no record at
    all, as at an Initialize, the record the merge adds names the providers instead: there is
    no earlier list to lower, and the run says so in a `NOTE` line. With a readable summary,
    the slot needs the provider it names, in that provider's place in the enabled list:
    `clear(<bot>)` only the first enabled provider, `fallback(<bot>)` only a later one, as the
    Merge summary's grammar gives them. Whether the earlier providers were unavailable stays
    for sessions to verify. Without a summary, the first enabled provider with a completed
    review fills the slot. At medium, after a successful bot policy read and parse,
    a readable summary with `reviewer=clear` and the agent account's successful
    `Reviewer` status on the head fills an unfilled slot
    only when `bot-1` declares `no-provider(none)` or `unavailable(<last enabled bot>)`,
    the last enabled bot in the base record's ordered list. An earlier unavailable provider
    or any other unfilled slot state stays missing. `no-provider(none)` declares exhaustion
    of an initially empty list or of all enabled bots; it does not prove requests occurred.
    Sessions verify actual requests and unavailability evidence. From v5 a declared
    `unavailable` or `no-provider` slot needs that medium substitution even with a slot
    waiver. With a known bot policy, either state at low or high records a missing bot.
    A low summary may omit the optional slot. `PROVIDERS` holds one reader per provider.
    Only enabled providers are read or reported.
  - **`reviewer`**: the agent account's newest `Reviewer` status on the head by merge time
    is `success`. From v5, on a medium merge changing fixed content or either instruction file,
    if Copilot alone completed an enabled bot review, require that status and a matching
    `reviewer=clear` entry. An owner waiver cannot supply either witness;
  - **`self-verification`** and **`security`**: the writer attests to completion. At high,
    summaries from v5 give the writer's security applicability decision on the third line.
    An applicable review needs a `security` declaration;
  - **a waiver** requires the repository owner's PR comment for one required item on
    the exact head, in the fixed form `WAIVER` reads. From v5, only a `waived` declaration
    can use it. The writer checks that the review was required and eligible for a waiver
    on this PR. A named bot must be enabled. At high, `security=waived` with
    `Security review applies: no` records a missing security review even with an
    exact-head security waiver.
    An omitted required row still yields `merge-summary` even when a waiver covers
    the underlying requirement. A v4 base keeps its published rule allowing a slot
    waiver to satisfy the required slot independently of its state.

  The repository owner is the owner in the repository's full name, a user account, as the
  generator requires. The Merge summary's writer checks waiver eligibility before merge.
  A body with no readable `Risk:` line is judged at high.

  A merge whose base record is below version 4, such as an Upgrade's own PR, follows that
  version's review rules. This script judges what every version requires: the Reviewer's
  status from medium, and a Merge summary for the tier and head with a `Required reviews:`
  line of any kinds. Its review bots follow rules this script doesn't hold, so they aren't
  judged, an accepted transition exception: that PR's Reviewer checks them before the merge,
  or its Builder does when an owner/exact-head `reviewer` waiver applies on a version 3 base.
  Versions 1 and 2 still require the Reviewer status; their transition rules are unchanged.
  The run says so in a `NOTE` line. An unsupported version or unreadable record leaves
  its policy unresolved. An omitted bot list leaves its order unknown; an empty list
  establishes that no bot was enabled.

  "No record" is GitHub's own answer for the path: HTTP 404 with the message `Not Found`
  (`NotFound`). Any other answer, a missing ref's 404 among them, is a read that failed. The
  workflow's token reads its own repository, so that answer can't mean the repository itself
  is out of reach. A base also holds no record after a merged PR deleted it, a change that
  reaches the record's own sensitive-path floor and is judged by the record before it.

On `workflow_run`, a push-triggered run on the default branch of any workflow but Merge watch
that concludes `failure`, `cancelled`, `timed_out` or `startup_failure` records an escape,
`red-default-branch`, naming the merged PR of the run's commit, unless such a record is
already open. Manual cancellation or a `cancel-in-progress` group on the default branch
may open a false record; that cost is accepted because a false record beats a lost one.

Review evidence is bounded by the PR's merge time. The historical record supplies the
agent identity for both the summary and the Reviewer status. Edited comment content that
cannot be reconstructed, missing timestamps and ambiguous Copilot check attribution are
reported as INCOMPLETE. The workflow posts independently supported misses and exits 1.
Copilot requires a submitted review and a successful check tied to its dynamic Actions
workflow, same head, job and check suite. A matching open miss issue must identify the miss in its
title and six opening fields. Exact observations deduplicate a rerun. A genuine open
red-default-branch record covers a continuing red branch. Two runs at once
can each read no open record, so two workflows failing together may open two
`red-default-branch` records: a concurrency group would cancel a pending run and lose its
record instead.

The `Risk:` and `Reverts:` lines and the record are read with the gate script's parser,
imported from beside this file. Python 3's standard library at the 3.9 level, plus `gh`.
"""

import argparse
from copy import copy
from datetime import datetime
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True

import gate  # noqa: E402

LABEL = "miss"
FOUND_BY = "Merge watch"
WORKFLOW = ".github/workflows/merge-watch.yml"
RECORD = ".github/governance/record.yml"

REVIEWER_CONTEXT = "Reviewer"

# The Merge summary header (docs/agents/review.md, Merge summary, On the PR).
SUMMARY_REVIEWS = "Required reviews: "
KINDS = ("self-verification", "bot-1", "reviewer", "security")
BOT_SLOTS = ("bot-1",)
MERGE_SUMMARY = "merge-summary"
REQUIRED = {
    "low": ("self-verification",),
    "medium": ("self-verification", "bot-1"),
    "high": ("self-verification", "bot-1", "reviewer"),
}
# A bot slot's state names its provider; `none` only when no enabled provider is left.
SLOT_STATES = {"clear": "provider", "fallback": "provider", "unavailable": "provider",
               "waived": "provider or none", "no-provider": "none"}
OTHER_STATES = ("clear", "waived")
_ITEM = re.compile(r"([a-z0-9-]+)=([a-z-]+)(?:\(([a-z]+)\))?")
NO_PROVIDER = "none"

# habit's waiver: the first line of a PR comment by the repository owner. The item is a
# review kind, or a row of the repository's verification table, which Merge watch doesn't judge.
WAIVER = re.compile("Waiver: (%s|verification \"[^\"\n]+\") at ([0-9a-f]{40}) \u2014 (\\S.*)" % "|".join(KINDS))

# A script can audit historical records up to its own rendered model version.
MODEL_VERSION = int("5")
# Version 4's ladder applies only when the merge's base has adopted it.
REVIEW_BOTS_VERSION = 4


class ReadError(Exception):
    """GitHub couldn't give a fact Merge watch reads."""


class NotFound(ReadError):
    """GitHub answered that the file isn't there: HTTP 404 with the message `Not Found`."""


UNKNOWN = object()


def unresolved(problems, message):
    if message not in problems:
        problems.append(message)
    return UNKNOWN


def read_rows(read, path, problems):
    try:
        rows = read(path)
    except ReadError:
        rows = None
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        return [unresolved(problems, path + ": list could not be read")]
    return [row if isinstance(row, dict) else unresolved(problems, path + ": malformed list member")
            for row in rows]


def record(merged_pr, kind, category, observed):
    """One miss record: its title, its six field lines and the `miss` label."""
    title = "Miss: %s, %s" % (kind, category)
    if merged_pr is not None:
        title += " in #%d" % merged_pr
    lines = (
        "Merged PR: %s" % ("#%d" % merged_pr if merged_pr is not None else "none"),
        "Kind: %s" % kind,
        "Category: %s" % category,
        "Observed: %s" % observed,
        "Found by: %s" % FOUND_BY,
        "Bug issue: none",
    )
    return {"title": title, "body": "\n".join(lines) + "\n", "labels": [LABEL]}


def _field(body, name):
    for line in (body or "").replace("\r\n", "\n").split("\n"):
        if line.startswith(name + ": "):
            return line[len(name) + 2:]
    return None


# The tracker permits free detail after a blank line following these six opening fields.
RECORD_OPENING = re.compile(
    r"Merged PR: (none|#[1-9][0-9]*)\nKind: (escape|process miss)\nCategory: ([a-z-]+)\n"
    r"Observed: ([^\n]+)\nFound by: (?:Merge watch|Planner|Builder|Reviewer|habit)\n"
    r"Bug issue: none(?=\n\n|\n?\Z)"
)
RED = ("failure", "cancelled", "timed_out", "startup_failure")


def _red_push(run, default_branch):
    path = run.get("path") or ""
    return (run.get("event") == "push" and run.get("conclusion") in RED
            and run.get("head_branch") == default_branch
            and isinstance(path, str) and path.partition("@")[0] != WORKFLOW)


def _red_incident(observed, repository, default_branch, read, problems):
    server = os.environ.get("GITHUB_SERVER_URL", "https://github.com").rstrip("/")
    prefix = re.escape(server + "/" + repository + "/actions/runs/")
    url = prefix + r"([1-9][0-9]*)"
    # A written non-red verdict cannot describe the open red incident.
    verdict = re.match(r"Workflow .+? concluded ([a-z_]+) on its push-triggered run ", observed)
    if verdict and verdict[1] not in RED:
        return False
    # The six fields identify an incident through its run and commit, however the
    # writer phrases the observation. Validate those facts for every author.
    pattern = r"(?:^|[\s(<])" + url + r"(?:/attempts/([1-9][0-9]*))?/?(?=$|[\s)>.,?#])"
    links = set(re.findall(pattern, observed, re.I))
    shas = set(re.findall(r"\b[0-9a-f]{40}\b", observed.lower()))
    if len(links) != 1 or len(shas) != 1:
        return False
    run_id, attempt = links.pop()
    sha = shas.pop()
    path = "repos/%s/actions/runs/%s" % (repository, run_id)

    def read_run(suffix=""):
        try:
            run = read(path + suffix)
        except ReadError:
            run = None
        if (not isinstance(run, dict) or str(run.get("id")) != run_id or not is_sha(run.get("head_sha"))
                or not all(isinstance(run.get(key), str) and run[key] for key in ("event", "head_branch", "path"))
                or "conclusion" not in run):
            unresolved(problems, path + suffix + ": could not verify the open red record's run")
            return {}
        return run

    run = read_run("/attempts/" + attempt if attempt else "")
    if run.get("head_sha") != sha:
        return False
    if attempt and str(run.get("run_attempt")) != attempt:
        return False
    if _red_push(run, default_branch):
        return True
    if attempt:
        return False
    # A bare run URL follows its latest attempt. A successful rerun does not close
    # the tracker record covering the earlier failed default-branch push.
    latest = run.get("run_attempt")
    if type(latest) is not int or latest < 1:
        unresolved(problems, path + ": could not establish the run attempt")
        return False
    for number in range(latest - 1, 0, -1):
        earlier = read_run("/attempts/%d" % number)
        if (earlier.get("run_attempt") == number and earlier.get("head_sha") == sha
                and _red_push(earlier, default_branch)):
            return True
    return False


def _record_key(title, body):
    opening = RECORD_OPENING.match(body.replace("\r\n", "\n"))
    if not opening:
        return None
    merged, kind, category, observed = opening.groups()
    expected = "Miss: %s, %s" % (kind, category)
    if merged != "none":
        expected += " in " + merged
    if title != expected or not observed.strip():
        return None
    return kind, category, merged, observed


def _open_records(read, repository, problems):
    issues = read_rows(read, "repos/%s/issues?labels=%s&state=open" % (repository, LABEL), problems)
    keys = set()
    for issue in issues:
        if issue is UNKNOWN or "pull_request" in issue or issue.get("state", "open") != "open":
            continue
        labels = issue.get("labels", [])
        if not isinstance(labels, list) or not any(
            label == LABEL or isinstance(label, dict) and label.get("name") == LABEL for label in labels
        ):
            continue
        if isinstance(issue.get("title"), str) and isinstance(issue.get("body"), str):
            key = _record_key(issue["title"], issue["body"])
            if key is not None:
                keys.add(key)
        elif issue.get("body") is not None or not isinstance(issue.get("title"), str):
            unresolved(problems, "open miss records: malformed issue")
    return keys


def is_sha(value):
    return isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", value) is not None


def _merged_into(pull, default_branch, sha):
    """Does this association establish a merge into the branch? Raise on an unresolved candidate."""
    base = pull.get("base")
    if not isinstance(base, dict) or not isinstance(base.get("ref"), str) or not base["ref"]:
        raise ValueError("missing base ref")
    if base["ref"] != default_branch:
        return False
    head = pull.get("head")
    if (type(pull.get("number")) is not int or pull["number"] < 1
            or not isinstance(head, dict) or not is_sha(head.get("sha"))):
        raise ValueError("invalid PR identity")
    squash = pull.get("merge_commit_sha")
    if "merged_at" in pull and pull["merged_at"] is None:
        if squash is not None and not is_sha(squash):
            raise ValueError("invalid merge_commit_sha")
        if pull.get("merged") is True or (squash == sha and pull.get("state") != "open" and pull.get("merged") is not False):
            raise ValueError("matching merge has no merged_at")
        return False
    if timestamp(pull.get("merged_at")) is None:
        raise ValueError("missing or invalid merged_at")
    if not is_sha(squash):
        raise ValueError("missing or invalid merge_commit_sha")
    if pull.get("merged") is False or pull.get("state") == "open":
        raise ValueError("merged_at conflicts with PR state")
    return True


def _merged_pr(read, repository, default_branch, sha, problems):
    """Return the matching merge; report direct push only if every association excludes a merge."""
    path = "repos/%s/commits/%s/pulls" % (repository, sha)
    matches = []
    possible_history = False
    for pull in read_rows(read, path, problems):
        if pull is UNKNOWN:
            possible_history = True
            continue
        try:
            merged = _merged_into(pull, default_branch, sha)
        except ValueError as error:
            unresolved(problems, "%s: unresolved PR association: %s" % (path, error))
            possible_history = True
            continue
        if merged:
            possible_history = True
            if pull["merge_commit_sha"] == sha:
                matches.append(pull)
    if matches and any(row["number"] != matches[0]["number"] for row in matches[1:]):
        unresolved(problems, path + ": conflicting exact PR associations")
        return [], True
    return matches, possible_history


def agreed(values, problems, source):
    """Only a disagreement between readable observations can contradict a known value."""
    if not values:
        return UNKNOWN
    first = values[0]
    if any(value != first for value in values[1:]):
        return unresolved(problems, source)
    return first


def possible_tiers(risks):
    if not risks:
        return set(REQUIRED)
    return {risk if risk in REQUIRED else "high" for risk in risks}


def merge_facts(matches, problems):
    """Preserve the risk observations for each reported (head, merge time) and the shared revert fact."""
    number = matches[0]["number"]
    revisions, reverts = {}, []
    for row in matches:
        key = (row["head"]["sha"], timestamp(row["merged_at"]))
        risks = revisions.setdefault(key, set())
        text = row.get("body")
        if "body" not in row or (text is not None and not isinstance(text, str)):
            unresolved(problems, "#%d: malformed PR body" % number)
            continue
        body = gate.parse_body(text or "")
        risk = body["risk"]
        risks.add(risk["tier"] if isinstance(risk, dict) else risk)
        reverts.append(body["reverts"])
    if len({head for head, _ in revisions}) > 1:
        unresolved(problems, "#%d: conflicting merged heads" % number)
    if len({when for _, when in revisions}) > 1:
        unresolved(problems, "#%d: conflicting merge times" % number)
    observed = set().union(*revisions.values())
    if len(observed) > 1:
        unresolved(problems, "#%d: conflicting risk declarations" % number)
    if len(observed) == 1 and all(revisions.values()):
        risk = next(iter(observed))
        declared = ("declared %s" % risk if risk in REQUIRED else
                    "declared no readable tier (its `Risk:` line is %s), judged at high" % risk)
    elif all(revisions.values()) and len(possible_tiers(observed)) == 1:
        declared = "risk declaration indeterminate, judged at high"
    else:
        declared = "risk tier indeterminate"
    return revisions, declared, agreed(reverts, problems, "#%d: conflicting revert declarations" % number)


def any_evidence(values):
    """A witness proves an existential claim. Only a complete negative proves absence."""
    uncertain = False
    for value in values:
        if value is True:
            return True
        if value is UNKNOWN:
            uncertain = True
    return UNKNOWN if uncertain else False


def timestamp(value):
    if isinstance(value, str):
        try:
            if value.endswith("Z"):
                value = value[:-1] + "+00:00"
            time = datetime.fromisoformat(value)
            if time.tzinfo is not None:
                return time
        except ValueError:
            pass
    return None


class Pull:
    """The historical policy and evidence for one PR. Every lookup is scoped to its merge."""

    def __init__(self, read, repository, number, head, cutoff, problems, notes, cache=None, squash=None):
        self.read, self.repository, self.number, self.head = read, repository, number, head
        self.prefix = "repos/" + repository
        self.cutoff = cutoff
        self.squash = squash
        self.problems, self.notes = problems, notes
        self._cache = {} if cache is None else cache

    def unknown(self, source, reason):
        return unresolved(self.problems, "#%d %s: %s" % (self.number, source, reason))

    def conditional_evidence(self):
        """Collect tentative reads separately until the condition needs them for a verdict."""
        facts = copy(self)
        facts.problems, facts.notes = [], []
        facts._cache = self._cache.copy()
        if isinstance(self.read, GitHub):
            facts.read = copy(self.read)  # Same transport and push deadline.
            facts.read.unreadable = facts.problems
        return facts

    def rows(self, endpoint):
        if endpoint not in self._cache:
            self._cache[endpoint] = read_rows(self.read, self.prefix + endpoint, self.problems)
        return self._cache[endpoint]

    def object_at(self, endpoint):
        if endpoint not in self._cache:
            try:
                value = self.read(self.prefix + endpoint)
            except ReadError:
                value = None
            self._cache[endpoint] = value if isinstance(value, dict) else {}
        return self._cache[endpoint]

    def matches(self, row, source, fields, *, by=None):
        """An identity mismatch or a known-late time excludes even a partially readable row."""
        if row is UNKNOWN:
            return UNKNOWN
        missing = []
        if by is not None:
            when = timestamp(row.get(by))
            if when is None or self.cutoff is UNKNOWN:
                missing.append(by)
            elif when > self.cutoff:
                return False
        for path, expected in fields.items():
            value = row
            for part in path.split("."):
                value = value.get(part) if isinstance(value, dict) else None
            if (type(value) is not type(expected) or value == ""
                    or (path in ("commit_id", "head_sha") and not is_sha(value))):
                missing.append(path)
            elif (value.lower() != expected.lower() if path.endswith(".login") else value != expected):
                return False
        if missing:
            return self.unknown(source, "missing or invalid " + ", ".join(missing))
        return True

    def by_merge(self, row, field, source):
        when = timestamp(row.get(field))
        if when is None or self.cutoff is UNKNOWN:
            return self.unknown(source, "cannot establish " + field + " at merge")
        return when <= self.cutoff

    def comment_bodies(self, login, newest_first=False):
        rows = self.rows("/issues/%d/comments" % self.number)
        source = "comments by " + login
        for row in (reversed(rows) if newest_first else rows):
            eligible = self.matches(row, source, {"user.login": login}, by="created_at")
            if eligible is False:
                continue
            if eligible is UNKNOWN:
                yield UNKNOWN
            elif self.by_merge(row, "updated_at", source) is not True:
                yield self.unknown(source, "pre-edit content cannot be established")
            elif not isinstance(row.get("body"), str):
                yield self.unknown(source, "malformed comment body")
            else:
                yield row["body"]

    def squash_parent(self):
        commit = self.object_at("/git/commits/" + self.squash)
        parents = commit.get("parents") if commit.get("sha") == self.squash else None
        if not isinstance(parents, list) or len(parents) != 1 or not isinstance(parents[0], dict):
            return self.unknown("policy", "could not establish the squash commit's parent")
        base = parents[0].get("sha")
        if not is_sha(base):
            return self.unknown("policy", "invalid squash parent")
        return base

    def record_at(self, ref):
        path = self.prefix + "/contents/" + RECORD + "?ref=" + ref
        if path not in self._cache:
            self._cache[path] = self.read(path)
        return self._cache[path]

    def policy(self):
        """Only the absence of the record at a verified parent permits the Initialize fallback."""
        base = self.squash_parent()
        if base is UNKNOWN:
            return UNKNOWN
        try:
            try:
                raw = self.record_at(base)
            except NotFound:
                self.notes.append("#%d merged onto a base with no governance record, so the record it adds names the enabled "
                                  "review bots." % self.number)
                raw = self.record_at(self.squash)
        except ReadError:
            return self.unknown("policy", "historical record could not be read")
        if not isinstance(raw, str):
            return self.unknown("policy", "invalid historical record")
        try:
            policy = gate.parse_record(raw.encode("utf-8"))
        except (gate.RecordError, UnicodeError):
            return self.unknown("policy", "invalid historical record")
        if policy["version"] > MODEL_VERSION:
            return self.unknown("policy", "unsupported historical version %d" % policy["version"])
        if policy["version"] >= REVIEW_BOTS_VERSION and "review_bots" not in policy["confirmed"]:
            self.unknown("policy", "historical record omits review_bots")
        return policy


# One reader per review bot: whether its review completed on the head, findings or not.
# Everything specific to a provider lives here (docs/agents/review.md, Review bots).

CODEX_LOGIN = "chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]"
CODEX_MARKER = re.compile(r"<!-- codex-review-state:v1 (\{.*?\}) -->", re.S)
COPILOT_LOGIN = "copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]"
COPILOT_CHECK = "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"


def _codex(pull):
    def completed(body):
        if body is UNKNOWN:
            return UNKNOWN
        for match in CODEX_MARKER.finditer(body):
            try:
                review = json.loads(match.group(1)).get("code_review")
            except (ValueError, AttributeError):
                continue
            if isinstance(review, dict) and review.get("commit_sha") == pull.head and review.get("status") == "completed":
                return True
        return False

    return any_evidence([completed(body) for body in pull.comment_bodies(CODEX_LOGIN)])


def _copilot_review(pull, review):
    source = "Copilot review"
    if review is not UNKNOWN and review.get("state") == "PENDING":
        return False
    identity = pull.matches(review, source, {"user.login": COPILOT_LOGIN, "commit_id": pull.head,
                                             "is_copilot_code_review": True}, by="submitted_at")
    if identity is not True:
        return identity
    state = review.get("state")
    if not isinstance(state, str):
        return pull.unknown(source, "missing review state")
    if state == "DISMISSED":
        return pull.unknown(source, "state at merge before dismissal cannot be established")
    if state not in ("COMMENTED", "APPROVED", "CHANGES_REQUESTED"):
        pull.notes.append("#%d Copilot has an unrecognized submitted review state." % pull.number)
        return False
    return True


def _copilot_check(pull, check):
    source = "Copilot check"
    match = pull.matches(check, source, {"name": COPILOT_CHECK, "status": "completed", "conclusion": "success",
                                         "head_sha": pull.head, "app.slug": "github-actions"}, by="completed_at")
    if match is not True:
        return match
    # The check links to a job and the job links back to the check. Fetch only same-repo
    # API paths built from their numeric IDs; the shared Actions app identifies no workflow.
    url = check.get("details_url")
    pattern = (r"https://github\.com/" + re.escape(pull.repository)
               + r"/actions/runs/([1-9][0-9]*)/job/([1-9][0-9]*)")
    link = re.fullmatch(pattern, url, re.I) if isinstance(url, str) else None
    suite = check.get("check_suite")
    if (not link or type(check.get("id")) is not int or check["id"] <= 0
            or not isinstance(suite, dict) or type(suite.get("id")) is not int or suite["id"] <= 0):
        return pull.unknown(source, "ambiguous producer: no matching Actions job and suite")
    run_id, job_id = link.groups()
    job = pull.object_at("/actions/jobs/" + job_id)
    check_url = "https://api.github.com/%s/check-runs/%d" % (pull.prefix, check["id"])
    if (type(job.get("id")) is not int or str(job["id"]) != job_id or type(job.get("run_id")) is not int
            or str(job["run_id"]) != run_id or job.get("head_sha") != pull.head
            or job.get("check_run_url") != check_url):
        return pull.unknown(source, "ambiguous producer: linked Actions job does not corroborate this check")
    run = pull.object_at("/actions/runs/" + run_id)
    if (run.get("id") != job["run_id"] or run.get("check_suite_id") != suite["id"]
            or run.get("head_sha") != pull.head):
        return pull.unknown(source, "ambiguous producer: linked Actions run cannot be corroborated")
    producer = pull.matches(run, "Copilot check (ambiguous producer)", {
        "event": "dynamic", "path": "dynamic/agents/" + COPILOT_CHECK, "actor.login": "Copilot",
    })
    if producer is False:
        pull.notes.append("#%d Copilot check belongs to a different Actions workflow." % pull.number)
    return producer


def _copilot(pull, *, presence_only=False):
    def witness(endpoint, qualifies):
        matches = (qualifies(pull, row) for row in pull.rows(endpoint))
        # A declared review reports unresolved siblings too. The companion needs
        # only one positive witness, which can avoid further Actions job reads.
        return any_evidence(matches if presence_only else list(matches))

    reviewed = witness("/pulls/%d/reviews" % pull.number, _copilot_review)
    if reviewed is False:
        return False
    endpoint = "/commits/%s/check-runs?check_name=%s&filter=all" % (pull.head, COPILOT_CHECK)
    checked = witness(endpoint, _copilot_check)
    return reviewed if checked is True else checked


PROVIDERS = {"codex": _codex, "copilot": _copilot}


def _reviewer(pull, agent_account):
    """GitHub lists statuses newest first. Ignore later postings, including later failures."""
    source = "Reviewer status"
    for row in pull.rows("/commits/%s/statuses" % pull.head):
        match = pull.matches(row, source, {"context": REVIEWER_CONTEXT, "creator.login": agent_account}, by="created_at")
        if match is False:
            continue
        if match is UNKNOWN:
            return UNKNOWN
        if row.get("state") not in ("success", "failure", "error", "pending"):
            return pull.unknown(source, "missing or invalid status state")
        return row["state"] == "success"
    return False


def parse_reviews(line, tier, *, require_minimum=True):
    """The `Required reviews:` line as {kind: (state, provider or None)}, or None when it doesn't read.

    It reads when every item is `<kind>=<state>`, a bot slot's state with its provider in
    parentheses, the kinds in their order and none twice, and it lists every kind the tier
    requires. V5 also reads individual declarations when a required kind is omitted.
    A provider is one `PROVIDERS` holds, or `none` where the state allows it, and
    `fallback` stands in `bot-1` at medium and high.
    """
    if not line.startswith(SUMMARY_REVIEWS):
        return None
    states, order = {}, []
    for item in line[len(SUMMARY_REVIEWS):].rstrip(" \t").split(", "):
        match = _ITEM.fullmatch(item)
        if not match or match.group(1) not in KINDS or match.group(1) in states:
            return None
        kind, state, provider = match.groups()
        if kind in BOT_SLOTS:
            allowed = SLOT_STATES.get(state)
            if allowed is None or provider is None:
                return None
            if provider == NO_PROVIDER and NO_PROVIDER not in allowed:
                return None
            if provider != NO_PROVIDER and (provider not in PROVIDERS or "provider" not in allowed):
                return None
            if state == "fallback" and tier not in ("medium", "high"):
                return None
        elif state not in OTHER_STATES or provider is not None:
            return None
        states[kind] = (state, provider)
        order.append(KINDS.index(kind))
    if order != sorted(order) or (require_minimum and any(kind not in states for kind in REQUIRED[tier])):
        return None
    return states


def _summary_lines(pull, agent_account, tier, version):
    """The lines of the agent account's newest Merge summary titled for the tier and the head, or None."""
    head = pull.head if version >= 5 else pull.head[:7]
    title = f"## Merge summary: {tier} at {head}"
    for body in pull.comment_bodies(agent_account, newest_first=True):
        if body is UNKNOWN:
            return UNKNOWN
        lines = body.replace("\r\n", "\n").split("\n")
        if lines[0].rstrip(" \t") == title:
            return lines
    return None


def _summary_reviews(lines, tier, version):
    if lines is UNKNOWN:
        return UNKNOWN
    return parse_reviews(lines[1], tier, require_minimum=version == 4) if lines and len(lines) > 1 else None


def waived(pull, owner):
    """A known owner waiver applies only to its named kind. An unreadable one proves nothing."""
    kinds, uncertain = set(), False
    for body in pull.comment_bodies(owner):
        if body is UNKNOWN:
            uncertain = True
            continue
        first = body.replace("\r\n", "\n").split("\n", 1)[0].rstrip(" \t")
        match = WAIVER.fullmatch(first)
        if match and match.group(2) == pull.head and match.group(1) in KINDS:
            kinds.add(match.group(1))
    absent = UNKNOWN if uncertain else False
    return {kind: True if kind in kinds else absent for kind in KINDS}


def earlier_version_missing(pull, agent_account, owner, tier, version):
    missing = []
    if tier != "low":
        waiver = waived(pull, owner)["reviewer"] if version == 3 else False
        if waiver is not True and any_evidence((waiver, _reviewer(pull, agent_account))) is False:
            missing.append("reviewer")
    lines = _summary_lines(pull, agent_account, tier, version)
    if lines is not UNKNOWN and not (lines and len(lines) > 1 and lines[1].startswith(SUMMARY_REVIEWS)):
        missing.append(MERGE_SUMMARY)
    return missing


def _bot_slot(pull, summary, bots, tier, agent):
    if bots is None:
        return UNKNOWN
    if summary is None or summary is UNKNOWN or "bot-1" not in summary:
        completed = any_evidence(PROVIDERS[bot](pull) for bot in bots)
        if summary is not UNKNOWN:
            return completed
        # Even unreadable declarations cannot supply a review when no provider completed
        # and a medium Reviewer substitution is impossible.
        if completed is False and (tier == "high" or _reviewer(pull, agent) is False):
            return False
        return UNKNOWN
    state, provider = summary["bot-1"]
    if state in ("clear", "fallback"):
        allowed = bots[:1] if state == "clear" else bots[1:]
        return provider in allowed and PROVIDERS[provider](pull)
    exhausted = ((state, provider) == ("no-provider", "none")
                 or (state == "unavailable" and bool(bots) and provider == bots[-1]))
    return (tier == "medium" and exhausted and "self-verification" in summary
            and summary.get("reviewer") == ("clear", None) and _reviewer(pull, agent))


def _declared_missing(pull, summary, bots, tier, agent, waivers):
    """Check each declaration against its own evidence, including reviews above the minimum."""
    missing = []
    for kind, (state, provider) in summary.items():
        if state == "waived":
            evidence = waivers[kind]
            if kind == "bot-1" and provider != NO_PROVIDER and bots is not None and provider not in bots:
                evidence = False
        elif kind == "bot-1":
            evidence = _bot_slot(pull, summary, bots, tier, agent)
        elif kind == "reviewer":
            evidence = _reviewer(pull, agent)
        else:
            continue  # The writer attests to a clear self-verification or security review.
        if evidence is False:
            missing.append(kind)
    return missing


def _high_security_missing(lines, summary, waiver):
    decision = lines[2].rstrip(" \t") if len(lines) > 2 else ""
    if decision == "Security review applies: no":
        return ("security",) if summary.get("security") == ("waived", None) else ()
    if decision != "Security review applies: yes":
        return (MERGE_SUMMARY,)
    if "security" in summary:
        return ()
    return ("security", MERGE_SUMMARY) if waiver is False else (MERGE_SUMMARY,)


# The whole fixed files and the two instruction files in the v5 manifest. Even
# the repository-owned part of an instruction file requires the companion.
V5_COMPANION_PATHS = {
    "AGENTS.md", ".claude/CLAUDE.md", ".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md",
    ".github/governance/branch_rules.py", ".github/governance/gate.py",
    ".github/governance/merge_watch.py", ".github/governance/owner.sh",
    ".github/workflows/governance-gate.yml", ".github/workflows/merge-watch.yml",
    "docs/agents/builder.md", "docs/agents/domain.md", "docs/agents/handoff.md",
    "docs/agents/issue-tracker.md", "docs/agents/planner.md", "docs/agents/review.md",
    "docs/agents/reviewer.md", "docs/agents/triage-labels.md",
}


def _fixed_record_changed(pull, base):
    try:
        before, after = pull.record_at(base), pull.record_at(pull.squash)
    except ReadError:
        return pull.unknown("merged change", "could not read both historical records")
    if not isinstance(before, str) or not isinstance(after, str):
        return pull.unknown("merged change", "invalid historical record content")
    old, new = before.split("\n"), after.split("\n")
    if old.count("confirmed:") != 1:
        return pull.unknown("merged change", "could not identify the fixed record at " + base)
    boundary = old.index("confirmed:") + 1
    if old[:boundary] != new[:boundary]:
        return True
    if any(line.strip() and not line.startswith((" ", "#")) for line in new[boundary:]):
        return pull.unknown("merged change", "unexpected top-level content after confirmed")
    return False


def _companion_change(pull):
    """Compare the squash to its verified parent. PR file lists can describe a different change."""
    base = pull.squash_parent()
    change = pull.object_at("/compare/%s...%s" % (base, pull.squash))
    files, commits, reported_base = change.get("files"), change.get("commits"), change.get("base_commit")
    if (not isinstance(reported_base, dict) or reported_base.get("sha") != base
            or type(change.get("total_commits")) is not int or change["total_commits"] != 1
            or not isinstance(commits, list) or len(commits) != 1
            or not isinstance(commits[0], dict) or commits[0].get("sha") != pull.squash
            or not isinstance(files, list)):
        return pull.unknown("merged change", "could not establish the squash comparison")

    # GitHub's compare endpoint returns at most 300 files across all pages. A
    # witness still counts at the limit, but absence needs a complete list.
    complete = len(files) < 300
    modified_record = False
    for row in files:
        if not isinstance(row, dict):
            complete = False
            continue
        status = row.get("status")
        if status not in ("added", "removed", "modified", "changed", "renamed", "copied"):
            complete = False
            continue
        paths = [row.get("filename")]
        if status == "renamed":
            paths.append(row.get("previous_filename"))
        for path in paths:
            if not isinstance(path, str) or not path:
                complete = False
            elif path in V5_COMPANION_PATHS:
                return True
            elif path == RECORD:
                if status not in ("modified", "changed"):
                    return True
                modified_record = True
    if modified_record:
        fixed = _fixed_record_changed(pull, base)
        if fixed is not False:
            return fixed
    if not complete:
        return pull.unknown("merged change", "changed file list is incomplete")
    return False


def _companion_missing(pull, bots, summary, agent):
    """Yield each proven absence before a subsequent historical read can exhaust the budget."""
    if not bots or "copilot" not in bots:
        return
    # A clear declaration already required the historical status in _declared_missing.
    if isinstance(summary, dict) and summary.get("reviewer") == ("clear", None):
        return
    problems = []

    def evaluate(reader):
        facts = pull.conditional_evidence()
        result = reader(facts)
        if result is UNKNOWN:
            problems.extend(facts.problems)
        return result

    others = evaluate(lambda facts: any_evidence(PROVIDERS[bot](facts) for bot in bots if bot != "copilot"))
    if others is True:
        return
    copilot = evaluate(lambda facts: _copilot(facts, presence_only=True))
    if copilot is False:
        return
    change = evaluate(_companion_change)
    if change is False:
        return
    if UNKNOWN in (others, change, copilot):
        for message in problems:
            unresolved(pull.problems, message)
        return
    if summary is not UNKNOWN:
        yield MERGE_SUMMARY
    if _reviewer(pull, agent) is False:
        yield "reviewer"


def missing_reviews(pull, agent_account, owner, tier, bots, version):
    """Establish ordinary misses first and defer any additional companion reads."""
    lines = _summary_lines(pull, agent_account, tier, version)
    summary = _summary_reviews(lines, tier, version)
    waivers = waived(pull, owner)
    minimum = REQUIRED[tier]
    missing = set()
    if version >= 5 and isinstance(summary, dict):
        missing.update(_declared_missing(pull, summary, bots, tier, agent_account, waivers))
        minimum = set(minimum).difference(summary)
        if minimum:
            missing.add(MERGE_SUMMARY)
        if tier == "high":
            missing.update(_high_security_missing(lines, summary, waivers["security"]))
    elif isinstance(summary, dict):  # Published v4 waiver and minimum rules.
        for kind in ("self-verification", "reviewer", "security"):
            if summary.get(kind) == ("waived", None) and waivers[kind] is False:
                missing.add(kind)
    elif summary is None:
        missing.add(MERGE_SUMMARY)
    if "bot-1" in minimum and waivers["bot-1"] is not True:
        slot = _bot_slot(pull, summary, bots, tier, agent_account)
        if any_evidence((slot, waivers["bot-1"])) is False:
            missing.add("bot-1")
    if "reviewer" in minimum and waivers["reviewer"] is not True:
        if any_evidence((_reviewer(pull, agent_account), waivers["reviewer"])) is False:
            missing.add("reviewer")
    companion = _companion_missing(pull, bots, summary, agent_account) if version >= 5 and tier == "medium" else ()
    return missing, companion


def _judge_pull(read, repository, matches, squash, notes, problems):
    records = []
    pull = matches[0]
    number = pull["number"]
    revisions, declared, reverts = merge_facts(matches, problems)
    if isinstance(reverts, dict):
        reverted, _ = _merged_pr(read, repository, pull["base"]["ref"], reverts["sha"], problems)
        records.append(record(
            reverted[0]["number"] if reverted else None, "escape", "revert",
            "#%d, merged as %s, reverted %s, and its body had a `Reverts:` line." % (number, squash, reverts["sha"]),
        ))
    elif reverts is not None and reverts is not UNKNOWN:
        records.append(record(
            None, "escape", "revert",
            "#%d, merged as %s, has a `Reverts:` line that doesn't read (%s), so the reverted PR is unknown."
            % (number, squash, reverts),
        ))
    # A missing body leaves all tiers possible. A readable sibling for the same
    # revision bounds them. Establish only absences common to every supported reading.
    cache = {}
    candidates = [(Pull(read, repository, number, head, cutoff, problems, notes, cache, squash), risks)
                  for (head, cutoff), risks in revisions.items()]
    first_pull, _ = candidates[0]
    policy = first_pull.policy()  # All candidate revisions share this squash parent.
    if policy is UNKNOWN:
        yield from records
        return
    version, agent = policy["version"], policy["agent_account"]
    bots = policy["confirmed"].get("review_bots")
    owner = repository.split("/", 1)[0]
    if version < REVIEW_BOTS_VERSION:
        notes.append("#%d merged onto a base whose record is at version %d; its review bots follow that version's "
                     "rules, which this script doesn't judge." % (number, version))
    judgments = []
    for facts, risks in candidates:
        tiers = possible_tiers(risks)
        for tier in REQUIRED:
            if tier not in tiers:
                continue
            if version < REVIEW_BOTS_VERSION:
                judgments.append((set(earlier_version_missing(facts, agent, owner, tier, version)), ()))
            else:
                judgments.append(missing_reviews(facts, agent, owner, tier, bots, version))
    # A terminal quota stop ends the push after this PR's proved record has been
    # offered for posting. Unvisited alternatives keep their ordinary misses.
    interruption = None
    try:
        for missing, companion in judgments:
            missing.update(companion)
    except PushIncomplete as error:
        interruption = error
    common = set.intersection(*(missing for missing, _ in judgments))
    if common:
        heads = sorted({head for head, _ in revisions})
        subject = ("Merged head %s" % heads[0] if len(heads) == 1 else
                   "Merged as %s (possible heads %s)" % (squash, ", ".join(heads)))
        kinds = [kind for kind in KINDS + (MERGE_SUMMARY,) if kind in common]
        records.append(record(number, "process miss", "missing-review",
                              "%s, %s, lacks: %s." % (subject, declared, ", ".join(kinds))))
    yield from records
    if interruption is not None:
        raise interruption


PUSH_COMMIT_LIMIT = 2048
PER_PAGE = 100


def _push_commits(event, read, repository, problems):
    before, after = event.get("before"), event.get("after")
    commits = event.get("commits")
    listed = {}
    if isinstance(commits, list):
        for commit in commits:
            sha = commit.get("id") if isinstance(commit, dict) else None
            if is_sha(sha):
                listed[sha] = None
            else:
                unresolved(problems, "push commits: malformed list member")
        if (is_sha(before) and is_sha(after) and len(commits) < PUSH_COMMIT_LIMIT
                and len(listed) == event.get("size", len(commits))
                and (after in listed or event.get("forced") or event.get("deleted") or before == after)):
            yield from listed
            return

    # A non-forced update to a different tip introduces that commit even when the
    # webhook omits it. A forced rewind can point at an already-reachable commit.
    if (event.get("forced") is False and not event.get("deleted") and before != after
            and is_sha(after) and after != "0" * 40):
        listed[after] = None
    location = "push range %s..%s" % (before, after)
    # Judge each witness before requesting another page. Even a quota stop on that
    # page cannot discard the events or comparison rows already accounted for.
    yield from listed
    if not is_sha(before) or not is_sha(after) or "0" * 40 in (before, after):
        unresolved(problems, location + ": no comparable before and after commits")
        return
    recovered = set()
    total = None
    path = "repos/%s/compare/%s...%s" % (repository, before, after)
    page = 1
    while True:
        try:
            comparison = read("%s?per_page=%d&page=%d" % (path, PER_PAGE, page))
        except ReadError:
            unresolved(problems, "%s: could not read comparison page %d" % (location, page))
            break
        base = comparison.get("base_commit") if isinstance(comparison, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(base, dict) or base.get("sha") != before:
            unresolved(problems, "%s: comparison page %d has no matching base" % (location, page))
            break
        count, rows = comparison.get("total_commits"), comparison.get("commits")
        if not isinstance(rows, list):
            unresolved(problems, "%s: missing comparison commits on page %d" % (location, page))
            break
        for row in rows:
            sha = row.get("sha") if isinstance(row, dict) else None
            if not is_sha(sha) or sha == before or sha in recovered:
                unresolved(problems, "%s: invalid or repeated commit on page %d" % (location, page))
            else:
                recovered.add(sha)
                if sha not in listed:
                    yield sha
        if type(count) is not int or count < 0 or total not in (None, count):
            unresolved(problems, "%s: invalid comparison total on page %d" % (location, page))
            break
        total = count
        if len(rows) < PER_PAGE or page * PER_PAGE >= total:
            break
        page += 1

    if (total is None or len(recovered) != total or not listed.keys() <= recovered
            or (total and after not in recovered) or event.get("size", total) != total):
        unresolved(problems, "%s: incomplete commit coverage; identified %d commits (comparison total: %s)"
                   % (location, len(recovered | listed.keys()), total if total is not None else "unknown"))


def _on_push(event, read, repository, default_branch, notes, problems):
    for sha in _push_commits(event, read, repository, problems):
        matches, in_history = _merged_pr(read, repository, default_branch, sha, problems)
        if matches:
            yield from _judge_pull(read, repository, matches, sha, notes, problems)
        elif not in_history:
            yield record(
                None, "process miss", "push-without-pr",
                "Commit %s was pushed to %s with no merged PR." % (sha, default_branch),
            )


def _on_workflow_run(event, read, repository, default_branch, open_records, problems):
    run = event["workflow_run"]
    if not _red_push(run, default_branch):
        return []
    incidents = [_red_incident(observed, repository, default_branch, read, problems)
                 for kind, category, _, observed in open_records
                 if (kind, category) == ("escape", "red-default-branch")]
    if any(incidents):
        return []
    sha = run["head_sha"]
    matches, _ = _merged_pr(read, repository, default_branch, sha, problems)
    return [record(
        matches[0]["number"] if matches else None, "escape", "red-default-branch",
        "Workflow %s concluded %s on its push-triggered run %s at commit %s."
        % (run.get("name"), run.get("conclusion"), run.get("html_url"), sha),
    )]


def decide(event_name, event, agent_account, read, notes=None, problems=None):
    """The miss records to open for one event.

    `read(path)` returns the JSON list GitHub gives for a REST path, every page joined (a
    check-runs answer's `check_runs`), a Git commit, comparison page or Actions object, or record text.
    Reads may raise ReadError. The legacy agent_account argument is ignored: each merge's
    historical record supplies its account. Return {title, body, labels} records, add
    observations to notes, and incomplete assessments to problems (or notes when omitted).
    """
    notes = [] if notes is None else notes
    problems = notes if problems is None else problems
    return list(_event_records(event_name, event, read, notes, problems))


def _event_records(event_name, event, read, notes, problems):
    """Yield each known miss so a large push can post it before reading the next commit."""
    repository = event["repository"]["full_name"]
    default_branch = event["repository"]["default_branch"]
    if event_name == "push" and event.get("ref") == "refs/heads/" + default_branch:
        open_records = _open_records(read, repository, problems)
        records = _on_push(event, read, repository, default_branch, notes, problems)
    elif event_name == "workflow_run":
        open_records = _open_records(read, repository, problems)
        records = _on_workflow_run(event, read, repository, default_branch, open_records, problems)
    else:
        return
    for rec in records:
        if _record_key(rec["title"], rec["body"]) not in open_records:
            yield rec


# The entry the workflow runs.

class PushIncomplete(Exception):
    """The audit must stop issuing requests and report the unjudged part of the push."""


def _rate_limit_delay(status, headers, body, attempt):
    if status not in (b"403", b"429"):
        return None
    retry = headers.get(b"retry-after", b"")
    remaining = headers.get(b"x-ratelimit-remaining")
    if (status != b"429" and not retry.isdigit() and remaining != b"0"
            and b"rate limit" not in body.lower()):
        return None
    reset = headers.get(b"x-ratelimit-reset", b"")
    delays = []
    if retry.isdigit():
        delays.append(int(retry))
    if remaining == b"0" and reset.isdigit():
        delays.append(int(reset) - int(time.time()) + 1)
    # GitHub asks for at least one minute without a supplied delay and increasing
    # backoff for repeated secondary limits. A non-rate-limit failure is never retried.
    if not delays or attempt:
        delays.append(60 * 2**attempt)
    return max(1, *delays)


class GitHub(object):
    """`read` through `gh api`, every page of a list; each path that couldn't be read is kept in `unreadable`."""

    def __init__(self, push=False):
        self.unreadable = []
        # Allow the 360-minute job to report incomplete coverage before it times out.
        self.deadline = time.monotonic() + 350 * 60 if push else None

    def request(self, path, *options, data=None):
        command = ["gh", "api"]
        if self.deadline is not None:
            command.append("--include")
        command.extend((*options, path))
        for attempt in range(8):
            if self.deadline is not None and time.monotonic() >= self.deadline:
                raise PushIncomplete("audit time budget exhausted at " + path)
            result = subprocess.run(command, input=data, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)
            if self.deadline is None or not result.stdout.startswith(b"HTTP/"):
                return result
            parts = re.split(rb"\r?\n\r?\n", result.stdout, maxsplit=1)
            if len(parts) != 2:
                return result
            head, result.stdout = parts
            if not result.returncode:
                return result
            status_line = head.splitlines()[0].split()
            status = status_line[1] if len(status_line) >= 2 else b""
            headers = {}
            for line in head.splitlines()[1:]:
                key, _, value = line.partition(b":")
                headers[key.lower()] = value.strip()
            delay = _rate_limit_delay(status, headers, result.stdout, attempt)
            if delay is None:
                return result
            if attempt == 7 or time.monotonic() + delay >= self.deadline:
                raise PushIncomplete("GitHub still rate limited the audit at " + path)
            print("NOTE GitHub rate limit: waiting %d seconds before retrying." % delay, flush=True)
            time.sleep(delay)

    def _json(self, path):
        result = self.request(path)
        try:
            if result.returncode:
                raise ValueError(" ".join(result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").split()) or "gh failed")
            return json.loads(result.stdout)
        except ValueError as error:
            self.unreadable.append("%s: %s" % (path, error))
            raise ReadError(path)

    def __call__(self, path):
        # All requests have the form repos/{owner}/{repository}/{endpoint}.
        endpoint = path.split("/", 3)[3]
        if endpoint.startswith("contents/"):
            return self._file(path)
        if endpoint.startswith(("git/commits/", "actions/jobs/", "actions/runs/", "compare/")):
            return self._json(path)
        items, page = [], 1
        while True:
            paged = "%s%sper_page=%d&page=%d" % (path, "&" if "?" in path else "?", PER_PAGE, page)
            data = self._json(paged)
            if endpoint.partition("?")[0].endswith("/check-runs"):
                data = data.get("check_runs") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(data, list):
                self.unreadable.append(paged + ": the answer isn't a list")
                raise ReadError(path)
            items.extend(data)
            if len(data) < PER_PAGE:
                return items
            page += 1

    def _file(self, path):
        """A file's text at a ref, from the contents API's raw form; NotFound on GitHub's own answer that it isn't there."""
        result = self.request(path, "-H", "Accept: application/vnd.github.raw")
        if result.returncode != 0 and _not_found(result.stdout):
            raise NotFound(path)
        try:
            if result.returncode != 0:
                raise ValueError(" ".join(result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").split()) or "gh failed")
            return result.stdout.decode("utf-8")
        except ValueError as error:
            self.unreadable.append("%s: %s" % (path, error))
            raise ReadError(path)

    def post(self, repository, rec):
        result = self.request("repos/%s/issues" % repository, "--method", "POST", "--input", "-",
                              data=json.dumps(rec, sort_keys=True).encode("utf-8"))
        return result.returncode == 0


def _not_found(stdout):
    """Whether gh printed GitHub's error body for a missing file: status 404, message `Not Found`."""
    try:
        data = json.loads(stdout.decode("utf-8"))
    except ValueError:
        return False
    return isinstance(data, dict) and data.get("status") == "404" and data.get("message") == "Not Found"


def main(argv=None):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Merge watch's miss records for the event in GITHUB_EVENT_PATH.")
    parser.add_argument("--post", action="store_true", help="open each record as a `miss` issue")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    with open(os.environ["GITHUB_EVENT_PATH"], encoding="utf-8") as handle:
        event = json.load(handle)
    event_name = os.environ["GITHUB_EVENT_NAME"]
    github = GitHub(push=event_name == "push")
    notes, problems = [], []
    found = failed = False
    try:
        for rec in _event_records(event_name, event, github, notes, problems):
            found = True
            print("MISS %s. %s" % (rec["title"], _field(rec["body"], "Observed")), flush=True)
            if args.post and not github.post(event["repository"]["full_name"], rec):
                print("FAIL opening the record %s" % rec["title"], flush=True)
                failed = True
    except PushIncomplete as error:
        unresolved(problems, "push range %s..%s: %s" % (event.get("before"), event.get("after"), error))
    for line in github.unreadable:
        print("UNREADABLE " + line)
    for line in notes:
        print("NOTE " + line)
    for line in problems:
        print("INCOMPLETE " + line)
    failed = failed or bool(github.unreadable or problems)
    if not found and not failed:
        print("No miss in this %s event." % event_name)
    return 1 if failed else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
